## Key architecture decisions recorded

### Runtime / graph boundary

The Cognitive Graph Runtime may be hosted inside this repo, in a sibling package, in a separate package, or in a future repo. Placement does not change the boundary rule:

```text
Cognitive Graph Runtime -> Capability Bus -> Capability Router -> Capability Service -> Backend Adapter
```

Forbidden graph access:

```text
graph -> workerBridge
graph -> llama_worker
graph -> backend adapters
graph -> raw model paths/projector paths
graph -> direct tool processes
```

### Graph bridge surfaces

The blueprint identifies the bridge as:

```text
Action Surface
Result Surface
Event Surface
Context Surface
Memory / Storage Surface
```

### MCP compatibility

MCP is recorded as both inbound and outbound:

```text
mcpServerAdapter   [future inbound MCP compatibility / public integration adapter]
mcpClientBackend   [future outbound MCP compatibility / backend adapter]
```

Both directions must cross the Capability Bus. MCP is not allowed to bypass policy, authorization, cancellation, tracing, or result normalization.

### Knowledge DB / recall substrate

Knowledge DB is not only a backend. It is a memory/recall capability family that may coordinate direct recall, soft recall, reranked candidates, and graph-linked recall.

Runtime Dev may provide:

```text
storage
indexing
query
link/reference operations
checkpointing
candidate recall
result persistence
```

The Cognitive Graph Runtime owns:

```text
interpretation
relevance
traversal policy
promotion/demotion
verification/locking meaning
contradiction handling
repair decisions
```

### Storage backend family

The blueprint explicitly avoids forcing memory into one DB shape.

Candidate backend family:

```text
vectorStoreBackend
graphStoreBackend
knowledgeStoreBackend
checkpointStoreBackend
documentStoreBackend
artifactStoreBackend
eventLogStoreBackend
keyValueStateStoreBackend
relationalMetadataStoreBackend
toolBackend
```

